  "question": {
    "text": "<p>From the compounds given below, number of compounds which give positive Fehling's test is</p><p>Benzaldehyde, Acetaldehyde, Acetone, Acetophenone,Methanal, 4-nitrobenzaldehyde, cyclohexane carbaldehyde.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In Fehling’s solution, the reaction between copper(II) ions and aliphatic aldehyde is represented as;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RCHO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>RCOO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Hence ,Acetaldehyde <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> Methanal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>HCHO</mi></mfenced></math>, and cyclohexane carbaldehyde </p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0045_f64e7d0d3737.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 130px;\"/></p><p>compounds  gives positive Fehling's test.</p><p>Hence, the answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}